# DRY (Don't Repeat Yourself)

All new or generated code must have a **single source of truth**. Do not copy-paste logic, constants, or structural patterns that already exist.

## Required

- Before writing a block, search the codebase for the same behavior and **reuse or extend** it.
- Extract a helper, function, constant, or type when the same logic appears (or would appear) in more than one place.
- Shared values (sizes, IDs, flags, strings, magic numbers) live in one named constant or existing header — never duplicated literals.
- Prefer calling an existing API over reimplementing it “just for this file.”

## Forbidden

- Near-identical functions that differ only by a name, type, or a few literals — parameterize instead.
- Duplicating a `switch` / `if` chain that already exists elsewhere.
- Copying a UI/editor snippet and tweaking it in a second window instead of sharing a control or helper.
- Re-declaring the same constant under a new name in another file.

## Allowed duplication

- Trivial one-liners that are clearer inline than behind a helper (e.g. a single null check).
- Code that only *looks* similar but encodes different domain rules — do not force a shared abstraction.
- Generated tables or data dumps that are the canonical source (do not invent a second generator unless asked).

## Example

```c
// BAD — same bound check copied
if (id < 0 || id >= FOO_COUNT) return;
if (id < 0 || id >= FOO_COUNT) return;

// GOOD
if (!IsValidFooId(id)) return;
```
